# docker/Dockerfile does `COPY . .`, so anything NOT listed here is baked into
# the web/bot/scheduler image layers — permanently, and readable by anyone who
# can pull, `docker save`, or exec into the image, even if the file is deleted
# later. Secrets must therefore be excluded here as well as in .gitignore;
# the two files are NOT interchangeable and drifting apart is easy to miss.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.envrc
.git
.githooks/
.github/

# The age PRIVATE key — the single thing that can decrypt every backup. It
# lives on the server at ./secrets/age_identity.txt because the weekly
# restore-drill container needs it (mounted read-only, chmod 600 — see
# README's backup setup). Without this line a `docker compose up -d --build`
# on the server would copy it into the image, handing anyone who can read
# that image both the encrypted dumps and the key that opens them, which is
# exactly the separation the whole backup design exists to maintain.
secrets/
*.pem
*.key
age_identity*.txt
*credentials*.json

# Keep private reports, browser captures, and local instructions out of images.
**/[Aa][Uu][Dd][Ii][Tt]*.md
**/АУДИТ*.md
**/Аудит*.md
**/аудит*.md
audits/
.playwright-mcp/
playwright-report/
test-results/
.claude/
.codex/
.agents/
.impeccable/
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
CLIENT_BOTS.md
DESIGN.md
HANDOFF.md
INSTRUCTIONS.md
POS-DESIGN.md
PRODUCT.md
**/*.local.md
**/*.log
logs/
data/
private/
exports/
**/*.sqlite*
**/*.db
**/*.sql
**/*.dump
**/*.backup
**/*.age
**/*.csv
**/*.tsv
**/*.xlsx
**/*.xls
